            <div xml:id="d593">

                <pb facs="0811" n="729" sameAs="frus:frus1925v02/pg729"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">703.5867/86</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Sweden</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Magruder</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Stockholm</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-07-20"><hi rendition="#italic">July 20,
                        1925</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received August 13.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 528</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the Department’s
                    instruction No. 134 of June 24, 1925 (File No. 703.5867/85), respecting the
                    discontinuance of the representation of American interests in Turkey by the
                    Swedish Government, I have the honor to report that I am in receipt of a note
                    from the Swedish Ministry for Foreign Affairs, a copy and translation of which
                    are herewith enclosed,<anchor n="7" xml:id="d593-f1"/> to the effect that the
                    Swedish Minister at Constantinople has been instructed to discontinue such
                    representation and to turn over to the American High Commissioner any records
                    and other property of the United States that may be in his charge.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alexander R.
                    Magruder</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
